      "abstract": "The Atlas of Regenerative Materials\n\nThe Atlas of Regenerative Materials is collecting knowledge and know-how on availability and use of regenerative materials for construction. Data is structured in 5 entities: Resource, Buidling Material, Construction Technique, Professionals and Buildings. Taxonomies for all entities and for buiding elements help filter the dataset. \n\nEvery entry consists at least of: - Title- Descriptive Text- Material Tag (Earth, Straw, Hemp, Wood, Stone, Other Fibres, Re-Used)- One multimedia item- Entry author\n\nWhere applicable, adress(es), relations to other entries or to taxonomy items, external links and other entity-specific details can be added, as well as further textual information.\n\nData on Zenodo\n\nHere on this repository we share and store snapshots every 12 months. The dataset consists of tables for each entity of the Atlas of Regenerative Materials and the authors as well as the taxonomies. Additionnally GIS data on resource potentials is available for Switzerland and parts of Europe as far as they are being produced.\n\nData structure from snapshots\n\n\n\nEntities: Here are all textual inputs and relations from the entries, grouped by entity\n\nFiles: Here lie all multimedia documents related to the entries\n\nTaxonomies: All taxonomies used for characterisation of the entries\n\n\nGIS Data to be added soon\n\n \n\n ",
