      "abstract": "General information\n\n\n\nAuthor info: Jules GRANDVILLEMIN, PhD Candidate, EPFL (https://orcid.org/0009-0009-4663-6120).\n\nDate of collection: 19 December, 2025.\n\n\n \n\nDescription\n\n\n\nThis dataset provides all the data needed to reproduce the results of a submitted article that evaluates the potential (i.e. possibilities) to practice sustainable mobility in a given area.\n\nTo do this, the author calculated three scores, the formulas and data used for each of which are listed in the \u0027Methodological info\u0027 section in the README.txt file:\n\n\n(i) a score for accessibility to essential daily human needs on foot or by public transport (PT);\n\n(ii) a score for individual motility, i.e. their ability to use PT;\n\n(iii) a synthetic score combining the two previous scores: i.e. accessibility and mobility.\n\n\n\nPlease note that, for ethical reasons, we removed the personal identifiers and residential locations of the surveyed individuals from the dataset. \n\nHowever, the results are reproducible because we:\n\n\n\nUsed the centre of 1580 x 1km² cells (where individuals\u0027 residences are located) as the origin of the travels to calculate the accessibility score, so their residence\u0027s localisation is not needed;\n\nTransmitted all the data used to obtain the results (file data) that we spatialised through the 1 km² cells (SMP_dataset.zip/data/results.gpkg).",
      "citation-key": "item_2a58173b223944ba82cf2d5e242cd424",
      "citation-label": "item_2a58173b223944ba82cf2d5e242cd424",
      "DOI": "10.5281/zenodo.22768812",
      "publisher": "Zenodo",
      "title": "Evaluating sustainable mobility potential: dataset",
      "URL": "https://infoscience.epfl.ch/handle/20.500.14299/267349"
    }
  ]
