      "abstract": "This dataset contains numerically generated correlated disordered patterns for metasurfaces and their simulated optical scattering responses. The structures consist of cylindrical or ring-shaped dielectric scatterers with a constant refractive index n \u003d 3.5 and height h \u003d 200 nm on a substrate of the same material. The dataset explores how the optical scattering response changes as the spatial-frequency content is controlled in single and superimposed metasurfaces.\n\nThe dataset is organized around comparing the collective scattering response of the metasurface to the forward-scattering efficiency, Qscat, of a single nanoresonator.The term \"CLR vs Qscat\" is used throughout the dataset as a naming convention for this comparison. It does not correspond to a directly stored variable in the data files. The raw simulation outputs contain wavelength-resolved power quantities (e.g., source power, transmitted power, and far-field power).\n\nThe analysis and visualization of the collective response (CLR) are performed through post-processing using the provided Jupyter notebooks and Python functions.\n\nQscat is provided separately as a reference dataset for isolated scatterers.\n\nMethodology for pattern generation and calculation can be found in the associated thesis.",
      "citation-key": "item_6369f69dcf1c4d44b81ee6461daa93ee",
      "citation-label": "item_6369f69dcf1c4d44b81ee6461daa93ee",
